course: dictionary
lesson: 12186
title: A formal word: conducive
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Conducive is a formal word. You will find it in exam questions, reports and serious writing. Conducive to something means it helps that thing to happen.
explain: «A quiet room is conducive to study.» Study is the thing being helped, so a quiet room helps you study. Ask: what would help here? Then try your meaning in the sentence. A quiet room helps study, so the meaning fits.
explain: The word to almost always comes after conducive. Look for the thing that gets helped after to. Teachers also use it: «A tidy classroom is conducive to learning.» Good for and helps are simple swaps you can try.
fact: Conducive means helping something to happen.
fact: Conducive is almost always followed by to: conducive to something.
fact: «A quiet room is conducive to study.» means a quiet room helps you study.
fact: Conducive is a formal word, so you will meet it in exams and serious writing.
fact: In science, warm, damp conditions are conducive to mould growth.
exercise: «Warm, damp air is conducive to mould growth.» What does conducive mean here? | Kills mould with cold | *Helps mould to grow | Makes mould smell nice | Stops mould from growing
exercise: Mrs Hale writes, «A calm, tidy classroom is conducive to learning.» What is she saying? | A calm, tidy classroom makes learning harder | Learning happens only in noisy rooms | A calm, tidy classroom has nothing to do with learning | *A calm, tidy classroom helps learning happen
exercise: In «Soft music is conducive ___ relaxing», which small word fits the gap? | for | of | *to | with
test: «The park was conducive to a long, happy picnic.» What does conducive mean here? | Was far away from the picnic | *Helped the picnic to be long and happy | Made the picnic cold and wet | Stopped the picnic from happening
test: Which sentence uses conducive correctly? | *Good light is conducive to reading. | Reading is conducive lights good. | Good light conducive is reading. | Conducive good light reading is.
exam: Pick the word that completes the sentence: «Soft music is ___ to sleep.» | curt | barely | *conducive | drooped
